# AEO Suite V3: AIOptimize Phase 1 Architecture, Manifest Specifications & Execution Plan

## 1. Executive Baseline & Governance Enforcement

* **Repository Active Branch**: `feature/ai-optimize` (branched from `dev` following the completed staging refactor of AI-Visualize).


* **Core File Protection Gate (Strict Freeze)**: Under zero circumstances may any task in Phase 1 modify `frontend/optimize.html`, `frontend/visualize.html`, `frontend/visualize.js`, `frontend/visualize.css`, `frontend/index.html`, `frontend/index.js`, or `frontend/index.css`. All Phase 1 capabilities must be engineered through backend services, API controllers, and isolated testing harnesses (`frontend/test-optimize-*.html` / `frontend/test-optimize-*.js`).


* **"AI-Optimized" Gate**: Applied strictly and exclusively to human-centric web presence, crawlability, and citation audits (`AIVisualize`).


* **"AI-Ready" Gate**: Applied strictly and exclusively to machine manifest hierarchies (`/robots.txt`, `/llms.txt`, `/ai-context.md`, and Level 1–4 files in `AIOptimize`).


* **Banned Terms Gate**: Complete and absolute ban on the term "AI-first" across all templates, comments, code, stylesheets, and test files.


* **Data Integrity & Zero-Fallback Gate**: Pre-scan inputs and state displays must show graceful defaults (`"--"`, `"UNAUDITED"`). Under no circumstances will synthetic mock fallbacks, static dummy payloads, or synthetic fallback data be injected into a user-requested output. Any extraction or crawl failure must surface an explicit error notification in the UI/dashboard and require user authorization to trigger a rescan.


* **DOM Pre-rendering Gate**: All educational copy, FAQ answers, and manifest cards must be pre-rendered in static HTML for LLM/bot crawlability.



